---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Speaking and mentorship"
  description="Mentorship, community programmes, hackathons and talks on product management, AI, compliance and automation."
>
  <section class="wrap wrap--prose page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Speaking and mentorship</p>
    <h1>Helping people make sense of complex work.</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I like helping people make sense of complex work, especially early in their careers.
        Most of what I share is not theory. It is what I have actually used: how to write
        clearly, how to frame a tradeoff, how to use data without hiding behind it, and how to
        build things that earn trust.
      </p>

      <h2>Mentorship</h2>

      <p>
        At Microsoft I have mentored six early-career product managers and engineers, work
        that contributed to a 75% return outcome. That involved project matching, regular
        feedback and coaching on stakeholder communication, with an emphasis on moving people
        from completing tasks toward exercising product judgment.
      </p>

      <p>
        Earlier in my Microsoft career I co-founded and coordinated an early-career mentorship
        programme in Europe for product managers and software engineers. The format gave new
        hires somewhere to talk honestly about the first ninety days, public speaking, career
        transitions, promotion readiness and how to build credibility inside a large
        engineering organisation.
      </p>

      <h2>Programmes and events</h2>

      <p>
        I organised a company hackathon with more than 200 participants spanning 11 divisions
        and 14 countries. I have led and contributed to learning sessions on AI, compliance
        and automation, including product management forums, bootcamp sessions, webinars and
        ask-me-anything conversations.
      </p>

      <h2>Talks</h2>

      <p>
        At <strong>TekNexus Africa 2024</strong> I spoke on a panel called Growing Your Value
        in the Tech Economy: Income, Impact and Influence, alongside other speakers working
        across the continent and the diaspora. It is the conversation I most often end up
        having privately with people I mentor, so it was worth having in public.
      </p>

      <p>
        I have also run webinar series and ask-me-anything sessions on product management and
        career transitions. Recordings and announcements are collected on the{' '}
        <a href="/sources#community">sources timeline</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Community</h2>

      <p>
        Outside Microsoft I have shared product management lessons with communities connected
        to Product School, iSpace, Impact Hub Accra and ProductDive Lagos. I came through
        <a href="https://meltwater.org/" rel="noopener">MEST</a> in Accra myself, so the
        pipeline from training programme to shipped product is not abstract to me.
      </p>

      <h2>Topics I am happy to speak about</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>Treating compliance as a product problem rather than a reporting problem</li>
        <li>Deterministic AI in regulated workflows, and what auditors actually require</li>
        <li>Adoption of internal platforms when users cannot leave</li>
        <li>Building regulated products in emerging markets</li>
        <li>Moving between founder, scale-up and enterprise contexts</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-block: var(--space-2xl) var(--space-3xl);
  }

  .page h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-title-lg);
    max-width: 20ch;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }
</style>
